Subject: [PATCH] arm64: Set link register when forcing a call through a signal handler.

wine-mono's mono fork, merge request !218 (Esme Povirk, merged 2026-06-01):
https://gitlab.winehq.org/mono/mono/-/merge_requests/218

Applied verbatim. Unity's 2022.3 branch has no Windows-ARM64 port of its own; wine-mono's arm64 Windows
port (merge requests 176, 195, 215, 218, 229, 236 and 237, in that order) is the base the ARM64EC layer
(0009) builds on.

diff --git a/mono/mini/exceptions-arm64.c b/mono/mini/exceptions-arm64.c
index 68db1b0c5ea7d92a96b27aff60bf02ab019ab16a..ac70d7e8ce18a5390ba5c8a064661ef1c21c0bdb 100644
--- a/mono/mini/exceptions-arm64.c
+++ b/mono/mini/exceptions-arm64.c
@@ -795,6 +795,7 @@ mono_arch_setup_async_callback (MonoContext *ctx, void (*async_cb)(void *fun), g
 void
 mono_arch_setup_resume_sighandler_ctx (MonoContext *ctx, gpointer func)
 {
+	ctx->regs [ARMREG_LR] = (host_mgreg_t)(MONO_CONTEXT_GET_IP (ctx));
 	MONO_CONTEXT_SET_IP (ctx,func);
 }
 
